---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const parts = ["Mein Name ist Johannes. Ich bin 16 Jahre alt. Ich ", {"verb": "kommen", "answer": "komme"}, " aus Stuttgart. Ich bin Schüler und ich ", {"verb": "gehen", "answer": "gehe"}, " jeden Tag in die Schule. Ich ", {"verb": "lernen", "answer": "lerne"}, " sehr viel für meine Tests. Meine Familie ist groß. Ich ", {"verb": "haben", "answer": "habe"}, " eine Mutter und einen Vater und drei Geschwister, einen Bruder und zwei Schwestern. Meine Mutter ", {"verb": "heißen", "answer": "heißt/heisst"}, " Anja, und mein Vater ", {"verb": "heißen", "answer": "heißt/heisst"}, " Sven. Mein Vater ", {"verb": "haben", "answer": "hat"}, " auch drei Geschwister. Meine Geschwister und ich ", {"verb": "haben", "answer": "haben"}, " deshalb viele Cousins und Cousinen. Mein Cousin Peter ", {"verb": "gehen", "answer": "geht"}, " auch in meine Schule, aber er ", {"verb": "lernen", "answer": "lernt"}, " nicht so viel wie ich."];
---
<Base title="Lesson 4 extension: spelling and verb practice" description="Practise spelling names, complete a German verb exercise, and learn useful phrases for asking how words are spelled."><div class="lesson-two"><header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap"><a class="back" href="/resources/german-lesson-4">← Back to lesson 4</a><p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 04 · EXTENSION PRACTICE</p><h1>Say it. Spell it.<br /><em>Make it stick.</em></h1><p class="intro">Put the alphabet into practice, then check your German verb forms.</p><p class="context">Complete the <a href="/resources/german-lesson-4">main alphabet lesson</a> first. This page contains follow-up tasks.</p><nav aria-label="Practice steps"><a href="#spell">01 Spell names</a><a href="#verbs">02 Complete the text</a><a href="#phrases">03 Useful phrases</a></nav></div></header><div class="wrap lesson-body">
<section id="spell" aria-labelledby="spell-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 / SAY IT ALOUD</p><h2 id="spell-title">Start with a familiar name.</h2><ol class="speaking"><li>Say the alphabet from memory. Use the <a href="/resources/german-lesson-4#listen">letter recordings</a> to review anything you find difficult.</li><li>Spell your first and last name in German. Then try the names of family members, friends or invented characters.</li><li>Ask a partner to write what they hear, then compare. On your own, record yourself spelling a name and listen again.</li></ol><p class="tip">Take your time. Aim for clear letter names before trying to spell faster.</p></section>
<section id="verbs" aria-labelledby="verbs-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / CHECK YOUR VERB FORMS</p><h2 id="verbs-title">Complete Johannes’ story.</h2><p>Type the correct present-tense form of each verb in brackets. Pay attention to who is doing the action.</p><p class="small">Need a reminder? Review <a href="/resources/german-lesson-4#practice">present-tense endings</a> and <a href="/resources/german-lesson-3-main#practice">haben</a>.</p><form id="verb-practice"><div class="fill-text" lang="de">{parts.map((part,i)=>typeof part==='string'?part:<label class="blank"><span class="sr-only">Verb {parts.slice(0,i+1).filter(p=>typeof p!=='string').length}: {part.verb}</span><input type="text" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" data-answer={part.answer} aria-describedby={`verb-feedback-${i}`} /><span class="verb-hint"> ({part.verb})</span><span id={`verb-feedback-${i}`} class="blank-feedback" aria-live="polite"></span></label>)}</div><div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p id="verb-score" role="status"></p></form><noscript><p>Interactive checking needs JavaScript. Answers in order: komme, gehe, lerne, habe, heißt, heißt, hat, haben, geht, lernt.</p></noscript></section>
<section id="phrases" aria-labelledby="phrases-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / WORDS TO TAKE WITH YOU</p><h2 id="phrases-title">Ask, listen, clarify.</h2><div class="dialogue"><p><strong lang="de">Können Sie das buchstabieren, bitte?</strong><br/>Could you spell that, please?</p><p><strong lang="de">Wie schreibt man …?</strong><br/>How do you spell …?</p><p><strong lang="de">Wie bitte?</strong><br/>Pardon? / Could you repeat that?</p></div><p><span lang="de">das Alphabet, die Alphabete</span> — alphabet; <span lang="de">der Buchstabe, die Buchstaben</span> — letter; <span lang="de">buchstabieren</span> — to spell; <span lang="de">schreiben</span> — to write.</p><p>Finish with a short exchange: ask someone’s name, ask them to spell it, and use one phrase above to clarify what you heard.</p><a class="next" href="/resources/german-async#e1">Return to the curriculum →</a></section>
<aside class="source"><h2>Source &amp; adaptation</h2><p>Adapted from <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l4/erw/">Grenzenlos Deutsch, Lektion 4: Erweiterung</a>, supplied as a saved-page ZIP, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. The verb-completion text is reproduced with spelling corrections to “Schwestern” and “Cousinen”; the exercise is rebuilt with local answer checking. Speaking tasks are adapted and English phrase meanings added. Reference audio remains in the main lesson. This page has no offline-saving feature.</p><p>Original funding: National Endowment for the Humanities and the Mansergh-Stuessy Fund for College Innovation. Ramzunā Languages is not affiliated with the original authors.</p></aside></div></div></Base>
<script>
const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#verb-practice');
form?.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();let score=0;const fields=form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input');fields.forEach(input=>{const answer=input.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase('de');const correct=input.dataset.answer!.split('/').includes(answer);if(correct)score++;input.setAttribute('aria-invalid',String(!correct));input.parentElement!.querySelector('.blank-feedback')!.textContent=correct?' ✓ Correct':answer?` → ${input.dataset.answer!.split('/')[0]}`:' — Enter a verb';});document.querySelector('#verb-score')!.textContent=`${score} of ${fields.length} correct. Review your answers and try again.`;});
form?.addEventListener('reset',()=>{form.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input=>input.removeAttribute('aria-invalid'));form.querySelectorAll('.blank-feedback').forEach(el=>el.textContent='');document.querySelector('#verb-score')!.textContent='';});
</script>
<style>
